## Why there is still no recording — SIT.7 cannot be captured here

Gates (a), (b) and (c) pass, so the stop rule does not fire. The seating is still
not recorded, because no compliant capture path exists on this machine:

- No system-audio loopback device. `ffmpeg -f avfoundation -list_devices` reports
  one input, "MacBook Pro Microphone"; `system_profiler SPAudioDataType` reports a
  single built-in output ("MacBook Pro Speakers") and no virtual, aggregate, or
  multi-output device. `/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL/` has no loopback driver.
  Reading `:default` input hangs and produces no file.
- No on-screen capture. `screencapture -x` returns "could not create image from
  display" (exit 1): the unattended shell holds no Screen Recording grant.
- Headless CDP screenshots are the only capture available, and headless is
  excluded by `filmed-seating.md`.

A microphone recording of room speakers is not a compliant substitute: it is not
the tab's audio and cannot be judged by ear for SND.M1/M2 or X1–X5.

`SIT.7` is also unrealized: `tools-situational.md` leaves its seam TBD, and no
technical-design seam or accepted ADR names a recording hook.
